- Riley!
- She's back.


00:05:57.607 --> 00:05:58.647
- Riley!
- Just keep going.


00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.191
I know you can hear me.


00:06:02.112 --> 00:06:04.650
Honestly, I don't know
what you were thinking.


00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:08.066
Sorry, Peg.
I said I was sorry.


00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:10.530
This parking lot
is where we set up.


00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.738
Everybody knows that.
From here to the Pottery Barn.


00:06:14.082 --> 00:06:15.948
We have earned this spot
because we sell


00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.580
more Firefly Christmas
baked cookies than anyone.


00:06:18.837 --> 00:06:19.897
Maybe if you actually
showed up


00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.607
to a den-mother meeting,
you'd know these...


00:06:21.631 --> 00:06:24.294
Well, not all of us can sit around
in our perfect little houses


00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:26.671
south of the Boulevard, Peg.
Some of us have to work.


00:06:30.557 --> 00:06:34.551
I will be lodging a formal grievance
at the next den-mother meeting.


00:06:34.644 --> 00:06:35.644
Okay, you do that.


00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:40.272
I don't think you're
Firefly Troop material.


00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.650
Either one of you.


00:06:42.444 --> 00:06:43.480
Come on, Penelope.


00:06:51.578 --> 00:06:52.898
What an asshole.


00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.360
- Don't say that.
- Well, she is.


00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.702
Well, maybe so. But still...


00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:00.660
You should've punched
her lights out.


00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:05.873
"Punched her lights out," huh?


00:07:06.635 --> 00:07:08.718
You can't go around
punching people who are jerks.


00:07:08.803 --> 00:07:10.294
Then you're just as bad
as they are.


00:07:11.473 --> 00:07:13.931
Mom, I know you took
the morning off work.


00:07:15.185 --> 00:07:17.222
Thanks, for trying to help me.


00:07:19.731 --> 00:07:21.313
Do you know
how amazing you are?


00:07:25.403 --> 00:07:28.146
Happy birthday. Get in the car.
Run, run, run. Go, go, go.


00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:30.927
Listen,
I wouldn't ask...


00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.235
When do you think?


00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.122
Next month.


00:07:38.208 --> 00:07:39.494
Right. Yeah, thanks.


00:08:01.272 --> 00:08:02.934
- Hi, Daddy.
- Hey, squirt.


00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:04.477
- Oh, how are you?
- Hey!


00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:05.648
- I'm good.
- Good.


00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:07.647
- I should be home by 4:30.
- Okay.


00:08:07.946 --> 00:08:09.882
Someone's gonna have a birthday party.


00:08:09.906 --> 00:08:11.346
The other kids
will be there by 4:00.


00:08:11.741 --> 00:08:13.221
Can you handle 30 minutes
on your own?


00:08:14.244 --> 00:08:16.361
- How many other kids?
- All my friends, Daddy.


00:08:16.871 --> 00:08:20.160
Chris North, everything in your life
has prepared you for this moment.


00:08:20.917 --> 00:08:22.408
Oh, hey, I'm late. Love you.


00:08:22.585 --> 00:08:23.646
- Love you.
- Love you. Bye.


00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.377
- Love you.
- Bye, guys. Bye!


00:08:25.672 --> 00:08:26.992
Come here, birthday girl.


00:08:30.468 --> 00:08:32.084
Hi, Mr. Watson.
I'm late. Sorry.


00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.740
Well, we'll talk about it later.
I gotta do some Christmas shopping.


00:08:34.764 --> 00:08:37.848
- And I need you to close today.
- Oh, today is actually...


00:08:37.934 --> 00:08:39.926
Dee Dee called in sick,
so you're closing.


00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.373
- It's my daughter's birthday...
- You asked for extra hours,


00:08:42.397 --> 00:08:44.639
I'm giving them to you.
You're closing.


00:08:50.488 --> 00:08:52.775
Are you sure, Mickey?
Are you really sure?


00:08:52.866 --> 00:08:55.306
- 'Cause don't put me in a situation...
- I got kids too, man.


00:08:56.327 --> 00:09:00.571
Ten minutes, our lives change.
Our kids' lives change.


00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:04.326
Nobody knows, nobody will know.
All you gotta do is drive.


00:09:04.419 --> 00:09:05.751
I'll take care
of everything else.


00:09:05.837 --> 00:09:07.624
I don't know, Mickey.
I don't know.


00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:10.669
You wanna get Riley
a house, right?


00:09:11.009 --> 00:09:12.295
Good school for Carly.


00:09:12.886 --> 00:09:15.094
This greasy-hand shit,
it's not gonna get you there, man.


00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:16.680
This will.


00:09:29.819 --> 00:09:30.819
Hi!


00:09:31.529 --> 00:09:32.529
I'm here.


00:09:33.031 --> 00:09:34.772
Happy Birth...


00:09:37.869 --> 00:09:38.869
Where's everybody?


00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.076
Nobody came.


00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:45.042
Nobody came?


00:09:53.968 --> 00:09:55.379
<i>Riley, Peg.</i>


00:09:55.678 --> 00:09:59.547
<i>Let's forget that little snafu in
the parking lot ever happened.</i>


00:09:59.641 --> 00:10:01.758
<i>We're having a little holiday
get-together today.</i>


00:10:01.976 --> 00:10:03.256
<i>Penelope invited
the whole class.</i>


00:10:03.937 --> 00:10:06.554
<i>I think Carly's invite must
have gotten lost in the mail.</i>


00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:10.604
<i>Feel free to stop by,
if you're not doing anything else.</i>


00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:14.111
<i>I'm sure you remember the address.
South of the Boulevard.</i>


00:10:14.364 --> 00:10:15.650
<i>Hope to see you guys.</i>


00:10:16.783 --> 00:10:17.783
Told you.


00:10:18.493 --> 00:10:20.075
You should've punched
her lights out.


00:10:30.421 --> 00:10:31.707
You know what, buddy?


00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:36.751
We don't need them anyway.


00:10:38.429 --> 00:10:39.465
It's your birthday.


00:10:39.681 --> 00:10:40.967
My birthday sucks.


00:10:41.224 --> 00:10:43.557
- Carly, language.
- It does.


00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.562
We're gonna go out for pizza.


00:10:50.358 --> 00:10:51.394
Um...


00:10:51.526 --> 00:10:53.206
We are, just the three of us.
It'll be fun.


00:10:53.444 --> 00:10:55.857
And then we're gonna go
to the Christmas carnival.


00:10:55.947 --> 00:10:58.064
- Yeah!
- Yes, the Christmas carnival.


00:10:58.158 --> 00:11:01.822
And when we get there,
we are gonna ride every ride,


00:11:01.911 --> 00:11:03.447
and play every game.


00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.539
We'll do all the virus- and germ-infested... Whatever.


00:11:06.749 --> 00:11:08.727
But I'm good with that. It's your birthday.


00:11:08.751 --> 00:11:10.413
- And then...
- Ice cream?


00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.536
- Ice cream.
- Ice cream. Yes!


00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.043
Heck, yes. Ice cream, yes.
As much as you want.


00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:18.547
All right, we're gonna have a big night.
Go get a jacket. Let's go, go, go.


00:11:18.636 --> 00:11:19.876
Yeah! I'll be ready
in a second.


00:11:26.269 --> 00:11:27.805
- I'm sorry. I just...
- Hey, hey...


00:11:30.064 --> 00:11:31.555
It's not always
gonna be like this.


00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:33.150
You promise?


00:11:34.652 --> 00:11:36.644
Yeah. I promise.


00:11:37.113 --> 00:11:38.113
Come here.


00:11:45.496 --> 00:11:48.309
<i>This is Mickey. I'm not
here right now. Please leave a message.</i>


00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:50.620
Mickey, hey, it's Chris.


00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:53.295
I'm out.


00:11:53.796 --> 00:11:54.877
I'm not risking it.


00:11:56.674 --> 00:11:57.881
It's not worth it, man.


00:11:58.801 --> 00:12:01.760
All right? Listen, I'm sorry.
Give me a call when you get this.


00:12:04.307 --> 00:12:05.743
- Where's your dad?
- He's out here.


00:12:05.767 --> 00:12:06.767
Oh, good.


00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:08.727
Carnival!


00:12:10.188 --> 00:12:11.188
All right.


00:12:11.898 --> 00:12:12.898
Here we go.


00:12:14.275 --> 00:12:17.018
- Carnival.
- Right.


00:12:23.326 --> 00:12:25.693
It's me. Is the boss around?


00:12:26.996 --> 00:12:28.203
I found the other one.


00:12:29.916 --> 00:12:32.875
Seriously,
you try to rip me off?


00:12:34.712 --> 00:12:37.625
Did you really think you were
gonna get away with it, Mickey?


00:12:39.467 --> 00:12:41.925
Hey, boss, it's for you.
It's Cortez.


00:12:46.849 --> 00:12:48.340
I have to take
this phone call.


00:12:49.185 --> 00:12:50.642
I hope you don't mind, Mickey.


00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.471
Talk to me. What you got?


00:12:54.565 --> 00:12:57.057
<i>I'm tailing the other guy.
What do you want me to do?</i>


00:12:57.527 --> 00:12:58.527
Smoke him.


00:12:59.821 --> 00:13:00.857
Make an example.


00:13:02.156 --> 00:13:03.156
A loud one.


00:13:08.162 --> 00:13:09.162
Mickey...


00:13:11.332 --> 00:13:12.493
This what you wanted?


00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:14.951
Huh?


00:13:15.044 --> 00:13:16.831
Is it gonna make
all your problems go away?


00:13:21.175 --> 00:13:22.256
Feels good, huh?


00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.757
Have some folding cash on you.


00:13:27.765 --> 00:13:28.765
Right?


00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:31.018
Right?


00:13:32.061 --> 00:13:33.061
Fucking <i>puto.</i>


00:13:40.153 --> 00:13:41.189
Wee!


00:13:41.279 --> 00:13:42.565
I'm the king!


00:13:53.124 --> 00:13:54.365
High-five!


00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.122
I kept my eyes open
almost the whole... Oh!


00:13:58.796 --> 00:14:00.162
Oh, I hope
I look smart.


00:14:00.256 --> 00:14:01.497
Aww.


00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:02.671
- Not so much.
- Look at me.


00:14:03.885 --> 00:14:04.885
You're a booger.


00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.382
- Pretty charming.
- Ice cream!


00:14:07.472 --> 00:14:08.588
Oh. Uh-oh.


00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:23.246
- Come on.
- We're coming, we're coming.


00:14:23.321 --> 00:14:24.361
Hey, what'll it be?


00:14:24.447 --> 00:14:27.155
Uh, two of your finest
Rocky Roads, and...


00:14:27.241 --> 00:14:28.732
Yes, and whatever
the little lady...


00:14:28.826 --> 00:14:30.533
Peppermint. Double scoop.


00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.060
And a peppermint
double scoop.


00:14:32.121 --> 00:14:33.349
- All right.
- It's her birthday.


00:14:33.373 --> 00:14:35.093
- Happy birthday to you.
- Thank you.


00:14:57.146 --> 00:14:58.933
- ...with the...
- Yeah, I agree.


00:14:59.565 --> 00:15:00.976
Goodness, look at that.


00:15:01.484 --> 00:15:02.565
Can I try that?


00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:05.383
- Do you like it?
- Mmm-hmm.


00:15:06.948 --> 00:15:08.940
- ...birthday, kiddo.
- Bye, sweetie pie.


00:15:15.581 --> 00:15:16.867
- I'll grab a napkin.
- Okay.


00:15:16.958 --> 00:15:17.958
Okay.


00:15:20.211 --> 00:15:21.647
- Do you mind?
- Yeah, you got it.


00:15:21.671 --> 00:15:23.511
- Thank you. Have a good night.
- Bye-bye.


00:15:27.301 --> 00:15:29.196
- I know.
- We're gonna have your birthday every day.


00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.220
Every day!


00:15:31.305 --> 00:15:32.762
Hey, make sure
we can get in the car.


00:17:20.665 --> 00:17:21.665
Ready?


00:17:26.087 --> 00:17:29.125
Adult female, 35 years old.
Gunshot wound to the head.


00:17:29.215 --> 00:17:31.502
Severe cerebral hemorrhaging,
vitals holding.


00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:33.510
Closing up.


00:17:35.012 --> 00:17:36.012
We're good.


00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.600
Can I take a look?


00:17:58.661 --> 00:18:00.118
It's messed up, I get it.


00:18:00.663 --> 00:18:03.997
But you need to get your game face on.
We got a job here, all right?


00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:09.752
Shit ain't easy
when it's a kid.


00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:12.292
It's not supposed
to be easy.


00:18:13.342 --> 00:18:15.379
That's the difference
between us and them.


00:18:35.197 --> 00:18:37.384
You were supposed to call
me the moment she woke up.


00:18:37.408 --> 00:18:39.636
You don't wake up from
a month in a medically-induced coma


00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:40.901
like flipping on
a light switch.


00:18:40.995 --> 00:18:42.486
The gunshot may have
missed her brain,


00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.349
- but the cerebral swelling...
- But she's gonna be all right?


00:18:48.836 --> 00:18:50.356
"All right"
is out of my hands.


00:18:51.005 --> 00:18:52.496
When her memory
returned, she...


00:18:53.299 --> 00:18:55.336
We had to restrain her
and she had to be sedated.


00:18:57.303 --> 00:18:58.464
Mrs. North...


00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:02.050
- My name is Detective Stan Carmichael...
- Detective.


00:19:02.642 --> 00:19:05.225
I've been waiting
to speak to you for a long time.


00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:09.974
I'm very sorry for your loss.


00:19:11.233 --> 00:19:15.147
Forgive me for jumping in so abruptly,
but we have three suspects in custody,


00:19:15.237 --> 00:19:17.103
who we otherwise
will have to release tomorrow.


00:19:17.198 --> 00:19:18.718
Detective, this is really
not the time.


00:19:18.824 --> 00:19:19.860
I...


00:19:20.451 --> 00:19:21.487
I can talk.


00:19:25.748 --> 00:19:29.492
We think that what happened
may be linked to your husband.


00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.788
There were rumors he was involved
in a plan to rob a drug dealer


00:19:34.423 --> 00:19:36.005
named Diego Garcia.


00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.962
He wouldn't have...
He wouldn't do that.


00:19:38.052 --> 00:19:39.884
No, yes,
you're absolutely right.


00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:42.212
We recovered a voicemail
on his friend's telephone.


00:19:42.306 --> 00:19:44.093
Your husband did refuse
to go along with it,


00:19:45.142 --> 00:19:48.852
but word had already gotten out,
and got back to Garcia.


00:19:50.981 --> 00:19:53.564
Now, an informant has given us
a very credible lead,


00:19:53.651 --> 00:19:55.358
but no witnesses
are willing to step up.


00:19:56.153 --> 00:19:58.645
We know everything,
but can't prove anything.


00:20:02.493 --> 00:20:05.281
Detective, I think
that's enough now.


00:20:08.332 --> 00:20:10.494
You get some rest,
Mrs. North. I'll come back.


00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:16.209
But I, uh, thought
you might wanna have this.


00:20:47.037 --> 00:20:48.037
I saw them.


00:20:50.916 --> 00:20:52.185
<i>All right, bring them out.</i>


00:20:52.209 --> 00:20:53.450
Let's go. Get in there.


00:21:11.771 --> 00:21:13.057
It's number five.


00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:15.521
Number five,
step forward.


00:21:20.154 --> 00:21:21.395
Take them out. Next group.


00:21:31.916 --> 00:21:32.916
Number three.


00:21:34.668 --> 00:21:36.028
Number three,
step forward.


00:21:40.466 --> 00:21:41.502
That's him.


00:21:47.515 --> 00:21:48.515
Four.


00:21:57.107 --> 00:21:58.143
Are you sure?


00:22:05.157 --> 00:22:06.489
Yes, I'm sure.


00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:14.406
Hey, thanks.


00:22:24.093 --> 00:22:25.253
What's the matter,
not hungry?


00:22:28.889 --> 00:22:30.130
Tell me what that is.


00:22:31.851 --> 00:22:34.685
That would be
a detective badge.


00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:36.807
That would be all they found
on the last cop


00:22:36.897 --> 00:22:38.433
who went after Diego Garcia.


00:22:40.317 --> 00:22:43.355
It was in his locker,
hanging in his locker here,


00:22:43.445 --> 00:22:45.983
inside Metro Homicide
Headquarters.


00:22:47.658 --> 00:22:49.069
Garcia has people
on the inside?


00:22:51.704 --> 00:22:55.368
Garcia has a nickname.
"La Guillotine."


00:22:56.125 --> 00:22:57.912
There's a reason
for that shit, Stan.


00:22:59.169 --> 00:23:03.004
Chris North didn't even rob Garcia.
He just considered it.


00:23:03.465 --> 00:23:06.333
And he's on the wrong side
of the grass with his kid.


00:23:07.344 --> 00:23:10.178
Whatever happens with this case,
let it happen.


00:23:10.264 --> 00:23:11.380
Don't be stupid.


00:23:11.849 --> 00:23:14.216
You'll only get dead
and it won't change anything.


00:24:03.901 --> 00:24:04.901
Hello?


00:24:10.115 --> 00:24:11.447
- Oh, Mrs. North.
- Who are you?


00:24:12.117 --> 00:24:13.797
I... I hope you don't mind
I let myself in.


00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:17.288
I'm a friend.


00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:19.076
Uh, do you...


00:24:19.166 --> 00:24:21.579
- Do you wanna have a seat?
- What do you want?


00:24:24.004 --> 00:24:25.586
Eviction notice.


00:24:25.673 --> 00:24:29.758
I can only imagine how awful
all of this has been for you.


00:24:29.843 --> 00:24:32.483
I mean, how does one even begin to
recover from something like that?


00:24:32.638 --> 00:24:33.754
Why are you here?


00:24:35.015 --> 00:24:36.051
I just, uh...


00:24:36.475 --> 00:24:38.307
I just wanna give you
a bit of advice.


00:24:41.188 --> 00:24:45.102
The road to recovery
has to begin somewhere.


00:24:46.110 --> 00:24:47.646
The recognition that, um,


00:24:49.905 --> 00:24:52.397
as gut-wrenching as it is,


00:24:53.951 --> 00:24:55.067
in the end,


00:24:56.495 --> 00:24:58.782
nothing's gonna bring
your family back.


00:25:00.749 --> 00:25:02.536
I know, and that's
the regrettable,


00:25:03.877 --> 00:25:05.368
yet unavoidable truth.


00:25:09.216 --> 00:25:11.458
Eventually,
maybe not right away,


00:25:11.552 --> 00:25:14.590
but eventually it'll be time
for you to move on.


00:25:15.597 --> 00:25:19.307
New place, new clothes,
new memories.


00:25:19.560 --> 00:25:20.596
Uh...


00:25:26.650 --> 00:25:27.766
A new life.


00:25:37.036 --> 00:25:38.072
What is this?


00:25:43.917 --> 00:25:45.453
Lorazepam. Lithium.


00:25:46.003 --> 00:25:47.915
- Risperidone? That's an antipsychotic.
- Hey!


00:25:51.967 --> 00:25:53.378
I think it's time
for you to leave.


00:25:53.469 --> 00:25:57.008
Maybe you've made a mistake.
Your memory is a little hazy.


00:25:57.890 --> 00:25:59.222
I'm just putting it
out there.


00:25:59.475 --> 00:26:02.718
Maybe you didn't see things the
way you thought you saw them.


00:26:03.020 --> 00:26:04.056
Hmm?


00:26:05.564 --> 00:26:09.353
Get out of my house.
Get out of my house! Get out!


00:26:12.154 --> 00:26:14.567
You think that
you're gonna have justice?


00:26:15.866 --> 00:26:17.357
Make them all pay?


00:26:19.745 --> 00:26:22.112
- They won't.
- Get the fuck out!


00:26:34.718 --> 00:26:38.428
Is there anything else you would
like to ask the witness, Mr. Anderson?


00:26:39.056 --> 00:26:40.672
One last question,
Your Honor.


00:26:41.016 --> 00:26:44.976
Mrs. North, just to clarify one point.
Did you see them get out of the car?


00:26:45.771 --> 00:26:46.771
No.


00:26:46.855 --> 00:26:47.891
Mmm.


00:26:48.315 --> 00:26:50.227
Did the car
ever stop moving?


00:26:51.485 --> 00:26:52.485
No.


00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:56.109
And yet you identified my
clients as the alleged shooters?


00:26:57.825 --> 00:26:59.677
- They did it.
- Objection, Your Honor.


00:26:59.701 --> 00:27:01.567
- Calls for legal conclusion.
- Sustained.


00:27:01.870 --> 00:27:04.112
Mrs. North, we're interested
in facts, not opinions.


00:27:04.206 --> 00:27:05.475
He just asked me a question
and I just answered.


00:27:05.499 --> 00:27:08.833
It's okay. You identified
my clients, correct?


00:27:09.128 --> 00:27:11.165
- Yes, I did. They did it!
- Okay. Okay.


00:27:11.255 --> 00:27:16.171
And are you currently on any
antipsychotic medications?


00:27:17.636 --> 00:27:18.672
What?


00:27:19.096 --> 00:27:21.509
- Lorazepam, lithium, risperidone...
- Wait.


00:27:21.598 --> 00:27:22.992
Is there anything else
that we should know about?


00:27:23.016 --> 00:27:24.097
Wait, that's not accurate.


00:27:24.184 --> 00:27:28.474
You identified not one, but three men in
a moving vehicle at night from 30 feet.


00:27:28.564 --> 00:27:30.208
- After a month in a coma...
- Well, I... I saw them.


00:27:30.232 --> 00:27:31.835
- ...and a mental breakdown...
- It's not something you forget...


00:27:31.859 --> 00:27:33.962
And under the influence of antidepressant
and antipsychotic medications.


00:27:33.986 --> 00:27:35.666
Excuse me!
He's not listening to me!


00:27:35.696 --> 00:27:38.530
Is it possible that your recollection isn't
what you thought it was?


00:27:40.367 --> 00:27:41.403
No.


00:27:45.664 --> 00:27:47.030
No further questions,
Your Honor.


00:27:47.499 --> 00:27:49.539
Wait, but you're not hearing me.
Can you help me out?


00:27:49.626 --> 00:27:52.118
You're the District Attorney.
Can't you do anything?


00:27:52.212 --> 00:27:53.481
I didn't even take
those pills...


00:27:53.505 --> 00:27:56.168
It is the opinion of this court
that in this preliminary hearing,


00:27:56.592 --> 00:28:00.836
the evidence is insufficient for
a juror to reasonably conclude


00:28:00.929 --> 00:28:03.091
that the State has met
its burden of proof.


00:28:04.099 --> 00:28:06.762
I see no reason to hold the
defendants over for trial.


00:28:18.488 --> 00:28:20.855
Wait a minute.
This can't be over.


00:28:21.325 --> 00:28:24.033
- These men killed my family.
- Mrs. North, you're excused.


00:28:24.119 --> 00:28:25.346
No, they killed my family!


00:28:25.370 --> 00:28:27.682
- You are excused, Mrs. North.
- This guy showed up in my house.


00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:28.947
No, I am not finished!


00:28:29.082 --> 00:28:31.269
- You are excused, Mrs. North.
- He offered me money!


00:28:31.293 --> 00:28:33.574
- No, no, no! I am not done!
- Mrs. North, you're excused!


00:28:33.629 --> 00:28:34.731
- They are killers!
- Mrs. North.


00:28:34.755 --> 00:28:35.940
- They're fucking killers!
- Bailiffs!


00:28:38.508 --> 00:28:40.340
Get away from me!
I'm gonna kill them!


00:28:54.024 --> 00:28:55.731
Bailiffs,
remove this woman.


00:28:57.736 --> 00:29:01.275
Mrs. North, I'm remanding you to a
mental-health treatment program.


00:29:02.157 --> 00:29:03.193
Next case.


00:29:13.710 --> 00:29:15.372
Why is she bleeding?
What happened?


00:29:16.213 --> 00:29:18.296
She wouldn't stop banging
her head into the bars.


00:29:22.261 --> 00:29:24.924
- She's all yours now.
- All right. Mrs. North?


00:29:25.305 --> 00:29:27.592
Riley, it's Detective Stan Carmichael.
Do you hear me?


00:29:28.100 --> 00:29:29.511
Hey, guys,
come on, come on.


00:29:29.601 --> 00:29:31.955
She saw her family get murdered and
the guys who did it just walked.


00:29:31.979 --> 00:29:33.015
How about you lighten up?


00:29:35.482 --> 00:29:37.474
Clear? One, two, three.


00:29:41.405 --> 00:29:44.364
- Where is she going?
- County General, psych hold.


00:29:44.866 --> 00:29:45.982
That place is a nightmare.


00:29:46.743 --> 00:29:48.703
<i>County General, psych hold.</i>


00:29:49.579 --> 00:29:51.299
<i>That place is a nightmare.</i>


00:29:53.166 --> 00:29:54.998
Hang on. Let me make a call.


00:30:00.424 --> 00:30:01.424
Hey!


00:30:03.969 --> 00:30:05.301
- You all right?
- Mmm. Yeah.


00:30:07.889 --> 00:30:08.889
Sorry.


00:30:38.628 --> 00:30:39.628
Well, you called it.


00:30:44.176 --> 00:30:45.212
She'll turn up.


00:30:45.677 --> 00:30:47.509
One way or another,
they always do.


00:31:11.661 --> 00:31:14.244
Carmichael, 3-8-7-7,
Gang Homicide.


00:31:28.637 --> 00:31:30.629
Don't you look
especially pretty this morning?


00:31:30.722 --> 00:31:31.838
Thanks for showing up.


00:31:32.349 --> 00:31:34.432
I've always been
a firm believer in beauty sleep.


00:31:36.436 --> 00:31:37.436
Pro tip.


00:31:38.980 --> 00:31:41.723
Wait until you're dead
before you embalm yourself.


00:31:46.446 --> 00:31:47.482
Well...


00:31:48.907 --> 00:31:49.988
That's new.


00:32:34.536 --> 00:32:36.573
- Good morning, Lisa. You got a minute?
- What?


00:32:36.663 --> 00:32:38.529
Somebody drove
a truck into a gun store


00:32:38.623 --> 00:32:40.615
out in San Bernardino
a couple of nights ago.


00:32:40.709 --> 00:32:44.077
The place was a class-three dealer,
military-grade stuff.


00:32:44.171 --> 00:32:46.663
ATF called us after reviewing
the security footage.


00:32:47.257 --> 00:32:50.216
It was a woman. They got a partial
frame of the suspect's face.


00:32:50.469 --> 00:32:52.085
Give it to
the DHS fusion center.


00:32:52.637 --> 00:32:54.797
Let them run it through their
facial recognition system.


00:32:55.056 --> 00:32:59.642
I did. Got a possible match from Customs
on a stowaway incident, container ship,


00:32:59.728 --> 00:33:01.720
at the Port of LA
three months ago.


00:33:02.355 --> 00:33:04.312
Uh, your name popped up
on the case file so I...


00:33:10.071 --> 00:33:11.071
Inman?


00:33:15.327 --> 00:33:16.327
Inman.


00:33:16.828 --> 00:33:17.944
Pull that in already?


00:33:18.580 --> 00:33:21.163
Uh, yeah, I did.
I put it on the top rack, if you need it.


00:33:26.630 --> 00:33:28.622
Are you maybe thinking
what I'm thinking?


00:33:36.139 --> 00:33:37.139
Carmichael.


00:33:39.392 --> 00:33:40.392
Who?


00:33:41.937 --> 00:33:43.018
Yeah, sure.


00:33:44.773 --> 00:33:46.810
- The FBI wants to talk to us.
- Feds?


00:34:49.462 --> 00:34:50.498
Oh.


00:34:50.589 --> 00:34:51.589
Sorry about that.


00:35:11.735 --> 00:35:13.351
Did you guys
run out of terrorists?


00:35:13.945 --> 00:35:16.437
How come the Feds care
about a squirrelly soccer mom?


00:35:16.656 --> 00:35:18.613
Didn't she smack you
in the head five years ago?


00:35:18.700 --> 00:35:20.532
Smacking dumbasses
ain't a federal offense.


00:35:20.827 --> 00:35:21.908
Ha-ha.


00:35:21.995 --> 00:35:23.236
Bank robbery is.


00:35:24.080 --> 00:35:26.948
The night Riley North got away
from you, she stole $55,000


00:35:27.208 --> 00:35:28.519
from the bank
where she was employed.


00:35:28.543 --> 00:35:31.752
Are we talking about the same
Riley North? Bank robbery?


00:35:32.422 --> 00:35:35.165
Mmm-hmm. She just disappeared,
completely off the grid,


00:35:35.425 --> 00:35:37.587
as if she just ceased to be.


00:35:37.677 --> 00:35:39.714
You're shitting me.
She wasn't the type.


00:35:39.804 --> 00:35:40.885
I agree.


00:35:41.097 --> 00:35:44.261
A woman with no priors,
even if her family is brutally murdered,


00:35:44.351 --> 00:35:47.014
doesn't just up and take
50-large and then take off.


00:35:47.562 --> 00:35:48.769
Got my attention.


00:35:54.152 --> 00:35:57.236
How many times did you
betray your oath, Your Honor?


00:35:59.324 --> 00:36:02.863
I think that you're so goddamn corrupt,
I don't even stand out.


00:36:05.413 --> 00:36:06.413
Wow.


00:36:07.957 --> 00:36:10.870
So, here's the deal.


00:36:10.960 --> 00:36:14.249
If you can tell me my name,
I'll let you live.


00:36:15.882 --> 00:36:18.875
I mean, you'll eat out of a tube the
rest of your life, but you'll live.


00:36:20.220 --> 00:36:21.220
You ready?


00:36:23.139 --> 00:36:27.725
Do you remember my name?


00:36:33.566 --> 00:36:35.273
Interpol tagged her
four months later.


00:36:35.694 --> 00:36:38.311
Used her real name
in a hospital in Hong Kong.


00:36:38.488 --> 00:36:43.074
Showed up with a dislocated
shoulder, facial fracture, ruptured spleen.


00:36:43.284 --> 00:36:44.946
- Car wreck?
- Don't know.


00:36:45.120 --> 00:36:46.920
She left before we could
have her apprehended.


00:36:47.122 --> 00:36:48.122
She vanished.


00:36:48.206 --> 00:36:50.326
Every now and then, a lead
trickles in from somewhere.


00:36:50.583 --> 00:36:52.495
Some we can almost substantiate,
some we can't.


00:36:53.128 --> 00:36:55.415
She's a shit magnet.
Why are you wasting our time?


00:36:56.089 --> 00:36:57.455
Then we found this
on YouTube.


00:37:05.682 --> 00:37:06.718
Wha...


00:37:06.808 --> 00:37:08.891
That's... That's Riley North?


00:37:09.144 --> 00:37:10.760
Herself,
in Europe last year,


00:37:10.895 --> 00:37:13.137
under one of the four
identities we tracked so far.


00:37:13.481 --> 00:37:15.768
She got really, really good
at staying off the radar.


00:37:15.859 --> 00:37:18.693
So she spends the last five
years bouncing around the world,


00:37:18.778 --> 00:37:22.271
learning how to get
into trouble. And?


00:37:22.532 --> 00:37:24.132
We don't exactly know
what she was doing.


00:37:24.159 --> 00:37:26.902
What we do know is that she
arrived in LA three months ago.


00:37:29.289 --> 00:37:32.748
Security cameras got this during
a gun-shop burglary a few days ago.


00:37:32.834 --> 00:37:34.575
She only took military-grade.


00:37:34.794 --> 00:37:38.128
Automatic rifles, high-capacity shotguns,
specific ammunition.


00:37:38.965 --> 00:37:41.332
She knew exactly
what she was looking for.


00:37:42.093 --> 00:37:43.093
She's back.


00:37:43.178 --> 00:37:46.137
And today, you found the three guys
that allegedly killed her family.


00:37:46.514 --> 00:37:48.881
Strung up, execution-style.


00:37:51.186 --> 00:37:52.643
Do you know
what the date is today?


00:37:52.729 --> 00:37:54.391
- Come again?
- The date.


00:37:54.981 --> 00:37:57.064
- What's today's date?
- It's December 21st.


00:37:58.526 --> 00:38:00.392
Five-year anniversary
of her family's murder.


00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:09.820
This stuff wrapped around
you is det cord, explosive rope.


00:38:10.455 --> 00:38:12.117
You can cut through
anything with this.


00:38:12.207 --> 00:38:15.120
Cut through trees,
it can cut through concrete...


00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:16.960
Corrupt judges.


00:38:32.602 --> 00:38:34.594
Watching someone
take everything from you...


00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:38.647
All you have,


00:38:39.984 --> 00:38:41.270
all you're ever gonna have,


00:38:42.570 --> 00:38:44.436
just gone.


00:38:45.949 --> 00:38:47.235
Hurts, doesn't it?


00:38:50.119 --> 00:38:51.860
And knowing
that it's all over,


00:38:52.705 --> 00:38:55.197
and there is nothing
you can do about it.


00:39:00.505 --> 00:39:03.748
You didn't serve justice,
Your Honor. But I will.


00:39:48.761 --> 00:39:50.798
Carmichael. Mmm-hmm.


00:39:52.390 --> 00:39:53.390
What?


00:39:54.642 --> 00:39:55.642
Okay.


00:39:56.686 --> 00:39:57.686
Thanks.


00:39:59.314 --> 00:40:00.805
Steven Goldman
and Robert Henderson,


00:40:01.107 --> 00:40:03.565
the DA and attorney at the hearing,
five years ago?


00:40:03.651 --> 00:40:04.651
Yeah.


00:40:05.028 --> 00:40:06.908
Goldman was found facedown
in his swimming pool,


00:40:06.988 --> 00:40:08.980
and Henderson's house
burned down with him in it.


00:40:09.073 --> 00:40:10.609
Last night, both of them.


00:40:11.034 --> 00:40:12.241
And that's not all.


00:40:12.827 --> 00:40:16.662
LAPD Bomb Squad is currently onsite at
the residence of one James Stevens,


00:40:16.748 --> 00:40:19.161
criminal court judge,
recently retired.


00:40:19.417 --> 00:40:21.534
Some sort of explosion
at his house.


00:40:22.253 --> 00:40:24.586
There's barely enough left of him
to fill an evidence bag.


00:40:25.673 --> 00:40:27.505
Don't think I need
to tell you who he was.


00:40:27.842 --> 00:40:29.208
We gotta go wide with this.


00:40:29.302 --> 00:40:31.134
APB, the media,
the whole deal.


00:40:47.779 --> 00:40:49.566
That looks good. Stack it up.


00:41:03.670 --> 00:41:04.980
We need to talk to you.


00:41:05.004 --> 00:41:06.495
- We have a problem.
- What?


00:41:10.885 --> 00:41:11.885
Just a minute.


00:41:13.888 --> 00:41:15.220
Our informant called.


00:41:16.140 --> 00:41:17.381
She got a judge
and, uh...


00:41:17.934 --> 00:41:19.266
And a lawyer we paid off.


00:41:19.602 --> 00:41:23.312
Smoked some of our homies, too.
The ones we sent to take out her husband.


00:41:24.148 --> 00:41:26.811
- When the fuck was this?
- Like, five years ago.


00:41:27.026 --> 00:41:28.026
Is there a problem?


00:41:29.195 --> 00:41:30.311
No, just, uh...


00:41:32.323 --> 00:41:35.907
Go and get Jessica out of the car.
Bring her in with a couple of drinks.


00:41:37.370 --> 00:41:38.406
And that thing?


00:41:41.708 --> 00:41:44.451
Put a paycheck on her head.
Call it a day.


00:41:51.884 --> 00:41:54.877
Some personnel stuff.
You know how it goes.


00:41:55.888 --> 00:41:58.175
- Got 10 more tons...
- Your bullshit ain't why I'm here.


00:41:58.766 --> 00:42:01.224
You know you shouldn't
play games with the cartel.


00:42:03.146 --> 00:42:05.138
I came to deliver a message
from my father.


00:42:15.700 --> 00:42:16.941
It's just a misunderstanding.


00:42:17.285 --> 00:42:18.947
One shipment goes missing,


00:42:19.704 --> 00:42:21.161
maybe it's a mistake.


00:42:21.706 --> 00:42:22.787
But two?


00:42:24.125 --> 00:42:25.161
In a week?


00:42:25.710 --> 00:42:27.201
You think I tried
to steal from you?


00:42:27.795 --> 00:42:29.707
That I lasted this long
by being stupid?


00:42:31.924 --> 00:42:33.916
Everybody wants
to be a big dog.


00:42:34.635 --> 00:42:37.878
Little dogs trying to eat
my food. That's all it is.


00:42:40.933 --> 00:42:41.933
Hey, baby.


00:42:59.327 --> 00:43:00.408
Get the fuck out of here.


00:43:05.833 --> 00:43:07.574
There's something
you need to remember.


00:43:13.049 --> 00:43:15.462
You are still a little dog.


00:43:16.385 --> 00:43:18.843
Don't let our business
be interfered with again.


00:43:56.717 --> 00:43:57.717
Who's that for?


00:43:59.887 --> 00:44:00.887
It's for you.


00:44:02.140 --> 00:44:03.140
Thanks.


00:44:06.435 --> 00:44:07.516
Is he okay?


00:44:08.437 --> 00:44:09.437
He drinks.


00:44:10.690 --> 00:44:12.898
I have to take care of him
sometimes.


00:44:14.026 --> 00:44:16.018
<i>Stop requested.
Please use rear...</i>


00:44:22.285 --> 00:44:23.776
Dad, come on.


00:44:25.621 --> 00:44:26.702
Bye.


00:44:27.915 --> 00:44:29.795
I told you
not to speak to strangers.


00:44:31.586 --> 00:44:34.454
Hey. Where'd you get
that shitty toy?


00:44:36.090 --> 00:44:37.090
Sit.


00:44:47.393 --> 00:44:49.635
- Give me your wallet.
- Okay.


00:44:51.772 --> 00:44:53.434
I'm gonna need you
to stand still, please.


00:44:57.904 --> 00:45:02.023
All right. Who do we have here?
"Bryan Hartley, 1214 Harlow Street."


00:45:03.659 --> 00:45:04.820
Open your mouth, Bryan.


00:45:07.914 --> 00:45:10.031
This is one of those
life-altering moments.


00:45:10.249 --> 00:45:11.660
Do I have your attention?


00:45:11.834 --> 00:45:12.950
Uh-huh.


00:45:13.586 --> 00:45:15.426
I want you to take your boy
Christmas shopping.


00:45:15.504 --> 00:45:17.962
I want you to give him
the time of his life.


00:45:18.591 --> 00:45:20.878
I want you to grow up
and be the father he deserves.


00:45:21.385 --> 00:45:23.798
- Do you understand me?
- I understand.


00:45:24.347 --> 00:45:25.747
- Say it again.
- I... I understand.


00:45:25.932 --> 00:45:27.548
- Do you swear?
- I swear.


00:45:27.642 --> 00:45:31.056
1214 Harlow.
I will never forget you, Bryan.


00:45:31.354 --> 00:45:32.354
Are we clear?


00:45:34.190 --> 00:45:35.271
- Yeah?
- Yes, ma'am.


00:45:35.358 --> 00:45:36.518
What are you
still doing here?


00:45:40.905 --> 00:45:41.986
Come on.


00:45:43.199 --> 00:45:44.399
You ever sell him
anything else


00:45:44.450 --> 00:45:46.191
and I will blow you
and this place to bits.


00:45:46.285 --> 00:45:47.485
- Do you understand?
- Mmm-hmm.


00:45:47.578 --> 00:45:49.114
- Do you have a car?
- Yeah.


00:45:49.205 --> 00:45:50.321
Give me the keys.


00:45:51.874 --> 00:45:53.035
Consider it a rental.


00:46:54.937 --> 00:46:57.520
Hey. You're in
the wrong place.


00:46:58.316 --> 00:47:00.356
- Oh, actually, I'm not.
- Get the fuck out of here.


00:47:33.642 --> 00:47:35.133
What's up, man?
What's going on?


00:47:35.978 --> 00:47:37.719
I'm about to get
this money, homes.


00:47:59.251 --> 00:48:01.618
<i>...in this normally
quiet upscale neighborhood.</i>


00:48:01.712 --> 00:48:03.169
<i>Maureen, can you tell us more?</i>


00:48:03.255 --> 00:48:05.542
<i>What do we know
about the suspected bomber?</i>


00:48:05.633 --> 00:48:08.467
<i>North is suspected to
have been behind today's bombing</i>


00:48:08.552 --> 00:48:11.511
<i>and of possibly killing
up to five others.</i>


00:48:11.722 --> 00:48:15.056
<i>Authorities believe her to be
armed and extremely dangerous.</i>


00:48:15.142 --> 00:48:18.977
<i>If you see her, please contact
police at the number on the screen.</i>


00:48:38.958 --> 00:48:40.665
...<i>so-called
"Sweet Killer."</i>


00:48:40.918 --> 00:48:42.955
<i>What could be expected
for their next move?</i>


00:48:43.421 --> 00:48:46.289
<i>What will the law enforcement
agencies respond with?</i>


00:48:50.010 --> 00:48:52.878
<i>We have enough experience now to
determine the unusual behavior...</i>


00:48:53.806 --> 00:48:55.006
What the fuck?


00:48:59.728 --> 00:49:00.728
Get the fuck out of here.


00:49:09.697 --> 00:49:10.697
Oh, shit!


00:50:01.332 --> 00:50:02.332
Jesus!


00:50:58.681 --> 00:51:00.263
- Hi.
- Oh, God.


00:51:00.891 --> 00:51:02.098
I have questions for you.


00:51:02.518 --> 00:51:03.975
- You're not busy, are you?
- No.


